 {:seon.task/name "the-standard-repl-tools"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: \"do whatever is the standard REPL experience for clojure but adapt all code to be optimized for jolt.\" Jolt's clojure.repl has doc, find-doc, apropos, dir, demunge; no source, source-fn or pst (stdlib/clojure/repl.clj: image-baked vars carry no :file); *1 and *e are always nil (seon.repl/eval-code never sets them). source reads the live var's definition text (kept at definition by the compiler events) and :file/:line sources embedded in the binary for platform and library code (Jolt jolt/repl-source); doc adds a bounded see-also (contract, callers, callees, reaching tests, tasks, branch vs main) from the db value; *1 *2 *3 *e per session replace the result/hN interns (repl.clj:108); the prompt's two lines teach them. Subsumes seon.repl/source-at-the-repl. Unblocked (worktree session context-v2, 2026-10-22): ``seon.program/definitions-from-the-compiler`` merged (the unit tap in `seon.program/tap`), and source (`my.agent/source-fn`, the branch first, then a library var's :file and :line), pst (`my.agent/pst`) and *1 *2 *3 *e per session (`seon.repl/eval-code`) merged with 982c70e and 0ac34d2, proven by `seon.repl-test/an-agent-repl-answers-what-a-clojure-repl-answers`. What remains: doc's bounded see-also (callers, callees, reaching tests, tasks), whose functions exist as `my.agent/callers` and `my.agent/callees`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/source-shows-the-exact-definition-mid-request
                      seon.repl-test/doc-names-callers-callees-and-reaching-tests
                      seon.repl-test/star-1-and-star-e-hold-the-last-value-and-error}}
