 {:seon.task/name "a-stable-prefix-is-sent-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Worktree session context-v2 (B0.2). Measured 2026-10-22 through the server on this worktree session's root: every model request sends `seon.context/system-prompt` (prose, 3.7 KB), then the first turn's whole current-state block, then the scrollback, then the whole block again (`seon.context/messages`), so the task, its plan, its references and its sections go out twice a turn, and the history-overflow note is appended to the first user message, changing the prefix every turn after overflow (audit notes/AUDIT-v1-to-next-2026-10-22.md 2.3). v1 sent stable attempt sections in the system message (about 8.5k tokens, cached) and small turn sections (about 0.75k) and saw 85-91% cache hits in runs 9-13. DeepSeek and OpenAI-compatible providers cache a byte-identical message prefix. Correct: the request is [system: the help page, the same for every agent] [user: the attempt's sections, the task, its plan, references, found helpers, sections and evidence, rendered from the attempt's first turn's basis] [the scrollback] [user: the turn's sections, the turn n of m, proofs, refused, test-run, your last reply, unmerged entries, the last evaluations and the dropped-turns note]. The first two messages are byte-identical across an attempt's turns, and nothing is sent twice. Replaces `seon.context/system-prompt` and the overflow note's edit of the first message; `seon.context/render` stays the one maker. The server's context (`seon.turn/context-block`) shows both user messages."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.context-test/the-prefix-stays-byte-identical-across-turns
                      seon.context-test/each-section-is-sent-once-per-request}}
